    "name": "Zubiri to Pamplona",
    "theme": "Emergence",
    "narrative": "The forest trail gives way to the outskirts of Pamplona and you walk into your first city on the Camino. The contrast is disorienting — from birdsong and river crossings to traffic lights and shop windows. You catch your reflection in glass and barely recognize the person looking back. Three days in and the city feels like a test: can you carry the quiet you found in the mountains through places that do not want you to be quiet?",
    "closing": "Who are you when you step out of the wilderness and back into the world?",
